> to unwield the pickax again, etc.  After all if we wanted the game to be 
> less hard then we wouldn't be fooling around with conducts.

Realistically though, the only reason applying a pick-axe causes a
wield is so that the dev team can screw you when the pick-axe is
cursed.  When you apply a unicorn horn (also usable as a weapon),
that DOESN'T cause a wield.

In real life, if I started running around digging with a pick-axe,
and got in a fight with someone in a bar, I wouldn't suddenly forget
I had a pick-axe in my hands and hit someone with it.  Or, if I tried
that as a defense in a murder trial, it wouldn't fly too well,
"I'm sorry your honor, I forgot I had this pick-axe in my hands,
I only meant to punch him really hard."  Granted, Nethack is not
meant to be a realistic depiction of life in all ways, however
things that match our real-life expectations tend to heighten
the immersion and identification with our character, whereas
things that violate our expectations in nonsensical ways tend
to upset the willing suspension of disbelief.  YMMV.


